_scratch_mounted heartbeat-on-every-tick contract.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.1889,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'wire its classified outcome into the recurring observability.sh metric path' and 'UNKNOWN stays distinct from NOT-IN-SERVICE but is still below the alarm threshold' and 'UNKNOWN remains distinguishable in the metric stream'","observability.sh:577-588 makes the heartbeat-on-every-tick rule load-bearing: 'Every heartbeat still publishes on EVERY tick including its 0 path, because bug bff5 reserves ABSENCE to mean the publisher died — under treat_missing_data = breaching that is what makes the dead-man construction trustworthy'","observability.sh:604-606 documents bug 5fb0 where a check that could not execute silently pinned a heartbeat and mis-reported state","The plan's alarm mirrors treat_missing_data=\"breaching\", so absence == breach == indistinguishable from a published -1 unless the publisher is required to emit -1 on the UNKNOWN path"],"finding":"The plan claims UNKNOWN (-1) 'stays distinct from NOT-IN-SERVICE' and 'remains distinguishable in the metric stream', but never specifies that the new gate_scratch_volume_in_service publisher must emit a value on EVERY recurring tick — including the UNKNOWN path and the case where the check itself cannot run — rather than going silent.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4414de7f2c42f69c","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Live work item 5 / AC6","norm_id":"n2c8943e10fe3ee3d","priority":0.8889,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The terraform show / lsblk join errors out on a tick: check emits nothing; alarm breaches via missing-data but operators see silence, not the -1 UNKNOWN signal the plan promised to keep distinct","A partial run classifies gate-scratch as UNKNOWN but the publisher skips emission on the non-IN_SERVICE path"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add to Live-work item 5 / AC6: 'The publisher emits the metric on every tick including the UNKNOWN and check-cannot-run paths (value -1), never silence; absence remains reserved to mean the publisher/timer/host is dead, per observability.sh heartbeat semantics (bff5/5fb0).'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"Add a test-coverage acceptance criterion for the extended classifier that asserts each classification branch (IN_SERVICE=1, NOT-IN-SERVICE=0, UNKNOWN=-1) maps to the correct emitted metric value, including the attached-but-unmounted and unresolvable-join cases.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["E5"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.0611,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'reusing/extending scripts/assert_volumes_in_service.py ... classifies volumes as IN_SERVICE / NOT-IN-SERVICE / UNKNOWN'","'values IN_SERVICE=1, NOT-IN-SERVICE=0, UNKNOWN=-1 ... UNKNOWN stays distinct from NOT-IN-SERVICE but is still below the alarm threshold'","Verification only states 'a code change that must pass local verification, Gerrit LLM-Review+1, Gerrit Verified+1, and submit' — no branch-level test named"],"finding":"AC6 introduces new classification/emit logic (extending assert_volumes_in_service.py to emit IN_SERVICE=1 / NOT-IN-SERVICE=0 / UNKNOWN=-1, where UNKNOWN must stay distinct from NOT-IN-SERVICE), but the plan names no test that exercises the distinct classification branches — only generic 'local verification' plus Gerrit Verified+1. The load-bearing new behavior (both 0 and -1 breach the alarm while UNKNOWN remains distinguishable in the metric stream) is untested by construction.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0fe82a77db25e6ab","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC6 / Verification section","norm_id":"n892120f3c13d6305","priority":0.8889,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A regression collapses UNKNOWN (-1) into NOT-IN-SERVICE (0) or vice versa and the suite stays green because no test asserts the three distinct classification outputs against the lsblk join","The attached-but-unmounted (NOT-IN-SERVICE) path emits the wrong value and goes unnoticed since only the happy IN_SERVICE state is exercised by the live volume"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"State that the extended assert_volumes_in_service.py gets unit tests covering the mounted (IN_SERVICE), attached-but-unmounted (NOT-IN-SERVICE), and unresolvable/missing-join (UNKNOWN) inputs, each asserting the emitted rebar/host:gate_scratch_volume_in_service value.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternati